Portuguese Wine Production

Portugal has long been a world leader in the production and export of wine=
=2E Of Portugal's eleven major wine regions, the Douro is by far the most s=
ignificant to fine wine production=2E But another more modern success story=
 in Portugal has to do with simple, sweet ros  table wines that are sold un=
der brand names like Mateus and Lancers=2E Although the heyday of simple ro=
ses may have passed, they remain popular worldwide and between these wines =
and Port, account for roughly 70% of Portuguese wine exports=2E

What is unique about Portugal is the very large number (upwards of 500) of =
indigenous grape varietals=2E Even most wine experts are unfamiliar with th=
e grapes that produce Port, Madeira or any other Portuguese wine=2E Older v=
ineyards are planted with multiple grape varietals and as a result, sometim=
es these field blends are so varied that identifying all of the grapes isn'=
t possible=2E When new vineyards are created, single plantings are now the =
norm=2E As modernization continues, Portugal is proving that in spite of a =
long history of contributions it still has undiscovered potential=2E

